<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch bonds end up, supported by 10-year tap sale.</title>
<headline>Dutch bonds end up, supported by 10-year tap sale.</headline>
<text>
<p>--------------------(Snapshot at 1530 GMT)----------------------</p>
<p>*CASH YIELDS (Dutch state loans)</p>
<p> June 1999 7.50 pct   107.11/21 (-0.02)   bid yield 3.54 (+0.01)</p>
<p> Feb  2002		114.23/31 (+0.07)		 4.80 (-0.01)</p>
<p> Feb  2007 5.75 pct    99.67/75 (+0.19)		 5.79 (-0.03)</p>
<p> Jan  2023		111.90/10 (+0.23)		 6.52 (-0.03)</p>
<p>*FUTURES</p>
<p> BUNDS (June )	 100.82 (-0.18)</p>
<p>TREASURIES (June )  108.69 (-0.50 vs pvs Dutch close)</p>
<p>*DM/NLG		    1.1247 (PREV 1.1245)</p>
<p>--------------------------(SPREADS)----------------------------</p>
<p>*DSLs versus Bunds  (pvs close)    *DSL curve     (pvs close)</p>
<p> 5 yr	 flat	 unchd	  10-2 yr  229     (229)</p>
<p> 10 yr	-0.13	-0.12	  10-5 yr  100     (100)</p>
<p> Long	 -0.18	-0.17</p>
<p>-------------------------( May 27 )-----------------------------</p>
<p>* Dutch bonds end slightly higher on Tuesday, as market ignores losses on surrounding markets. Market supported by tap sales of second tranche of ten-year benchmark, dealers say short covering creates floor to prices in similar maturities as well. State collects 1.9 billion guilders under the programme today.</p>
